# This template needs no env vars for the local flow — your chain's RPC lives in
# l1.config.json (written by `pnpm l1`), and you connect with a browser wallet.
#
# On local networks, import avalanche-cli's public EWOQ dev key into your wallet
# — it's pre-funded on your chain. `pnpm l1` prints it when it finishes; it is
# also on the "ewoq" row of `avalanche blockchain describe <your chain name>`.
# It is not written in this file because secret scanners flag committed keys,
# even public dev ones. LOCAL ONLY.
#
# For the Fuji path (`pnpm l1:fuji`), bring your own funded Fuji wallet — never a
# real private key in this file.
